A||N||5||Bob Englert||Happiness is a good alignment!||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||03-30-2001||06:00 PM||||I just wanted to share with all that my blue 87 GT is finally driving like it was meant to!<P>After rebuilding the entire front suspension over the winter I took the car to what was supposed to be an experienced alignment shop.  I had nothing but problems and they never did make a serious effort to properly align the car.  I finally demanded and got my money back after they left the car with badly out of spec caster on the right side.  The car would take off to one side or the other at almost any rut in the road.  It was a real bear to drive over old asphalt highways.<P>I took the car to Piedmont Truck Tire in Greensboro today and had them mount new front tires and new rear struts along with a complete alignment.  The tech told me when I picked the car up that he could not believe how far out the car was.  He said the settings on either side were basically fighting each other for control over the car.  That was exactly how it felt on the road.<P>The before and after numbers if anyone is interested:<BR>Left Front:       Before     After<BR>Camber            0.8 deg    0.9 deg<BR>Caster            3.4 deg    5.2 deg<BR>Toe               -.34 deg   .14 deg<P>Right Front:      Before     After<BR>Camber            0.4 deg    0.4 deg<BR>Caster            0.9 deg    4.5 deg<BR>Toe               -.53 deg   .16 deg<P>Left Rear         Before     After<BR>Camber            1.0 deg    -1.0 deg<BR>Toe               -2.55 deg  .18 deg<P>Right Rear        Before     After<BR>Camber            0.1 deg    -1.0 deg<BR>Toe               -1.11 deg  .20 deg<P>Based on the printout values, I think the tech almost nailed the values.  It really drives like it now.<P>The moral of the story is that just because a shop has an alignment machine doesn't mean they know how to use it.  No Fiero should wander down the road or feel squirly or unsafe at speed unless you have worn suspension parts.  If you don't think you have gotten a good alignment, talk to the shop and MAKE SURE YOU GET THE SPECS from the machine.  Also remember that alignment machines need to be calibrated periodically, and even with 'good' specs you still might have a problem if the machine is out of whack.<P>Sorry for the long post, I am finally enjoying driving this car!<P>I'm excited (can you tell?)!!!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ben84||03-30-2001||06:41 PM||||Words of Wisdom... =0)<BR>I plan on a complete alignment this weekend.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Quadfiero||03-30-2001||07:43 PM||||Thanks for passing on the good word on that shop. I am almost willing to drive to Greensboro to get mine done. I have had problems in the past with alignment shops and it would be worth a little extra to know the job was done right. It really helps to know about these people that do good work. Helps eveyone out.<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Bob<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||03-30-2001||08:31 PM||||I swear, Columbus is one of the ten largest cities in the country, and I'll be damned if I can find a shop around here that can do an alignment, or even give me a decent tire balancing for that matter. In ten years, I've yet to find a competent shop for those services. Guess that's why I do *EVERYTHING* else myself....and if I could do those two things......||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||03-30-2001||08:39 PM||||I got lucky when I took mine to the Monro shop in Hazelton, PA.  I've had good luck with other cars there even though though they aren't the cheapest.  I'd rather pay a bit more and get a good job.  The tech was a former Fiero owner was happy to see and drive a Fiero, and even went for a ride with me to make sure it was right.||||reg||10
Z||000005||Bob Englert||03-30-2001||08:48 PM||||This shop was a pleasure to do business with.  They asked me if I wanted to drive the car before I paid the bill.  The tech told me if it still didn't feel right to bring it back and they could try to do some fine tweeking to adjust it further.  Just a first class shop all around.  I called them back at the end of the day to let them know how pleased I was.  I asked the counter guy I spoke with to pass it on the the tech.<P>My other GT will be there as soon as the suspension work is finished.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
